{"activity_text": "Anti-Gram+ & Gram-, Antifungal, candidacidal, Antibiofilm", "article_id": "", "assay_text": "Rich", "assay_type": "", "comments_text": "Sequence analysis: APD analysis reveals that this sequence is similar (63.64%) to HHC-48 W: 55%; K: 45%. GRAVY: -2.26, mol Wt: 1776.143; mol formula: C96H128N22O12; mol ex coeff: 33300. Activity: active against Gram+ S. aureus ATCC 25923A (MIC 25 uM), S. epidermidis ATCC 12228 (MIC 3.12 uM), B. megaterium Bm 11 (MIC 0.75 uM), Gram- bacteria A. baumannii ATCC 19606 (MIC 50 uM),, P. aeruginosa (MIC 3.12 uM), E. coli ATCC 25922 (MIC 6.25 uM), P. aeruginosa ATCC 27853 or 19595 or 4 clinical strains (MIC 1.56-6.12 uM), and yeast C. albicans ATCC 24433 (MIC 6.25 uM). Bactericidal effect. It inhibited biofilm formation:P. aeruginosa as gauged by biomass (CV) and metabolic activity. MOA:bacteria:S. epidermidis: MOA:bacteria:P. aeruginosa: MOA:fungi:C. albicans: the peptide showed membrane permeabilizaiton. Resistance development:no:bacteria:P. aeruginosa 19595: the clinical isolate P. aeruginosa 19595 did not develop clear resistance to the peptide (MIC change 2 fold) or colistin (MIC change up to 4 fold) after 15 passages. In vitro toxicity: showed minimal toxicity to HaCaT cells (20% viability decrease at 25 uM and 25% decrease at 50 uM).", "concentration": "", "cytotoxicity_text": "", "hemolytic_activity_text": "", "measure_group": "", "measure_value": "", "pubmed_id": "36465859", "record_granularity": "entry_text", "reference_text": "Front Chem. 2022 Nov 17;10:1000765. doi: 10.3389/fchem.2022.1000765. PubMed", "sequence_key": "APD6:AP04848", "source_id": "AP04848", "source_numeric_id": "04848", "source_path": "APD6/apd6_export/structured/peptides.csv", "source_record_id": "AP04848", "source_table": "peptides.csv", "stability_text": "", "subject_name": "", "target_organism_text": "", "title": "KDEON WK-11: A short antipseudomonal peptide with promising potential.", "unit": "", "﻿database": "APD6"}
